<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσελ-αύνω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσελ-ελάω</span></b> : fut.
			-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ελάσω <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>,</span>
		
			Att.
		 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ελῶ</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drive in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμὴν εἰσελάων [τὴν ποίμνην]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.83
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππους δ᾽ εἰσελάσαντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.385
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν θήλειαν ὁ ἄρρην εἰ. πρὸς τὰ
					ᾠά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.962f
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσελαύνειν τινὰ εἰς τὸν τοῦ
				πράγματος δρόμον</span>
			<i>to keep</i> him to the point, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.176
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.206
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as if intr.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθ᾽ οἵ γ᾽ εἰσέλασαν [τὴν
			νῆα]</span> that way they <i>rowed in,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				13.113
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ εἰσήλασεν εἰς τὴν πόλιν
				[τὸν ἵππον]</span> when he <i>marched into.</i>., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.2.26
			</span></i>, etc.: c. acc. loci, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. λιμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.672
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1265
			</span></i> ; <i>enter in triumphal procession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθρίππῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Publ.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὰς Ἀθήνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					12.58
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσελαύνειν θρίαμβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Mar.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Mi.</u>
				31
			</span></i>.</div>
